# 贪吃蛇 · 看懂 AI 的大脑

**{{AUTHOR}}**（{{AUTHOR_EMAIL}}）· {{UNIVERSITY_EN}} · {{UNIVERSITY_KO}}
代码 MIT · 文档与教学素材 CC BY 4.0

一个卷积神经网络用 Double DQN 学会了玩 10×10 的贪吃蛇。打开网页，你能实时看到它**在看哪里、每一层在想什么、为什么往这边拐**，还能亲手“敲掉”它的神经元，或者和它在同一局里比一比。手机、电脑都能直接用，不用安装、不用联网。

**English summary.** *Snake · Inside the AI's brain* is a browser-only teaching demo. A small convolutional network ({{PARAMS}} parameters), trained with Double DQN in PyTorch, plays Snake on a 10×10 grid; the page runs the real float16 weights in plain JavaScript and shows a live brain panel (input planes, the most influential convolutional channels, the fully connected layer, Q values and their contributions, plus a gradient saliency overlay). You can knock out neurons, play the same game against the DQN and replay the moves where you disagreed, or follow a guided practice checklist. Works on phones (portrait layout with a floating joystick) and desktops, online or from a downloaded zip. UI and documentation are in Chinese.

![观战模式：左边是蛇，右边是网络的实时“大脑”](docs/img/watch_1920x1080.png)

